{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And it shall be a double portion.</b> For the day and for the morrow." "<b>A double portion.</b> Because they were accustomed to gather each day of the rest of the week; I say \"which they shall bring, and it shall be double\" — after they bring it, they will find double in the measure compared to what they gather and measure each day. And this is \"they gathered bread, a double portion\" — at its gathering it was found to be bread, a double portion. And this is \"therefore He gives you on the sixth day bread for two days\" — He gives you a blessing, פוי\"שן, in the house, to fill the measure twice for bread of two days."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {1 "the la'az פוי\"שן is Old French poison/poson, 'portion' (here 'blessing in the measure' — the double portion received on Friday)"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:38.968684901Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}